/*!
 * \mainpage StChain — STAR Reconstruction and Analysis Chain
 *
 * \section intro Overview
 *
 * StChain is the backbone of the STAR software framework.  Every reconstruction
 * algorithm and analysis task is implemented as a **maker** — a concrete subclass
 * of StMaker — and executed by StChain inside a uniform event loop.  The chain
 * pattern separates the concerns of I/O, reconstruction, calibration, and analysis
 * into independent, composable units that can be assembled at runtime without
 * recompilation.
 *
 * \section pattern The Maker Pattern
 *
 * A maker is a self-contained processing module that:
 *  - declares its dependencies on other makers' outputs through named TDataSet keys,
 *  - performs its work inside Make(),
 *  - posts its results back onto the shared white-board (a TDataSet tree) so
 *    downstream makers can consume them.
 *
 * Makers are arranged in a tree whose root is an StChain instance.  StChain walks
 * the tree depth-first, calling each maker's lifecycle methods in the correct order.
 *
 * \section lifecycle Init / Make / Clear / Finish Lifecycle
 *
 * | Method          | When called                          | Typical use                                  |
 * |-----------------|--------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|
 * | Init()          | Once, before the event loop          | Open files, book histograms, allocate objects |
 * | InitRun(run)    | At the start of each new run         | Re-read calibrations, reset run counters     |
 * | Make()          | Once per event                       | Reconstruction and analysis                  |
 * | Clear()         | After each event                     | Reset transient data, free per-event memory  |
 * | FinishRun(run)  | At the end of each run               | Finalise run-level summary objects           |
 * | Finish()        | Once, after the event loop           | Write output, close files, print summaries   |
 *
 * \section new_maker Writing a New Maker
 *
 * Derive from StMaker, override the lifecycle methods you need, and post your
 * output onto the white-board:
 *
 * \code{.cpp}
 * #include "StMaker.h"
 *
 * class MyMaker : public StMaker {
 * public:
 *     explicit MyMaker(const char *name = "MyMaker") : StMaker(name) {}
 *
 *     Int_t Init() override {
 *         // Book histograms, open auxiliary files, etc.
 *         AddHist(new TH1F("hPt", "Track p_{T};p_{T} (GeV/c);counts", 100, 0, 10));
 *         return kStOK;
 *     }
 *
 *     Int_t Make() override {
 *         // Retrieve input data posted by an upstream maker.
 *         TDataSet *evt = GetDataSet("StEvent");
 *         if (!evt) return kStWarn;   // non-fatal: log and skip
 *
 *         // ... process event ...
 *
 *         return kStOK;
 *     }
 *
 *     Int_t Finish() override {
 *         // Histograms are written automatically; add any final printout here.
 *         return kStOK;
 *     }
 *
 *     ClassDef(MyMaker, 0)
 * };
 * \endcode
 *
 * Register the maker with the chain before calling Init():
 *
 * \code{.cpp}
 *   StChain *chain = new StChain("myChain");
 *   new StMuDstMaker(chain, ...);   // upstream I/O maker
 *   new MyMaker(chain);             // our custom maker
 *   chain->Init();
 *   chain->EventLoop(1, 500);
 *   chain->Finish();
 * \endcode
 *
 * \section event_loop How StChain Orchestrates the Event Loop
 *
 * StChain::EventLoop(jBeg, jEnd) drives the following sequence for each event
 * number \e n in [jBeg, jEnd]:
 *  -# If the run number changed, call FinishRun(oldRun) then InitRun(newRun) on
 *     every maker in the tree.
 *  -# Call StChain::MakeEvent(), which calls Make() on every maker depth-first.
 *     Processing stops early if any maker returns kStEOF or kStFatal.
 *  -# Call Clear() on every maker to release transient per-event data.
 *
 * \section data_flow Data Flow and StEvent
 *
 * Makers communicate through the white-board, a TDataSet tree managed by the
 * top-level StChain.  The central payload is **StEvent** (package StEvent), a
 * collection of tracks, vertices, hits, and detector-specific containers.
 *
 *  - **Input makers** (StIOInterFace subclasses) read raw or reconstructed data and
 *    post an StEvent onto the white-board under the key `"StEvent"`.
 *  - **Reconstruction makers** retrieve `"StEvent"`, add or modify collections
 *    (e.g. TPC hits, global tracks), and re-post it.
 *  - **Analysis makers** read `"StEvent"` in read-only fashion and fill histograms
 *    or ntuples.
 *
 * Conditions-database access is provided through StMaker::GetDataBase(), which
 * queries the STAR calibrations database keyed by logical path and event timestamp.
 *
 * \section classes Key Classes
 *
 * | Class              | Role                                                        |
 * |--------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
 * | StMaker            | Abstract base class for all makers                          |
 * | StChain            | Top-level chain controller; drives the event loop           |
 * | StIOInterFace      | Abstract base for I/O makers (MuDST, XDF, ROOT trees, …)   |
 * | StRTSBaseMaker     | Abstract base for makers that read raw DAQ data             |
 * | StEvtHddr          | Per-event header (run/event numbers, trigger masks, timing) |
 *
 * \sa StMaker, StChain, StIOInterFace, StRTSBaseMaker, StEvtHddr
 */
